These are my impressions after some time with 3.1 (maybe tiny spoilers):

Abut the game balance and playing style: 3.1 has much more levels and
therefore much more junk laying around. With the new formulae for carrying
capacity I usualy end up with full inventory quite early in the game (in
3.0 I can't remember this ever happening to me - and I had quite a few
ascensions). Now I am usually walking with several bags, because I
accumulate interesting stuff faster than I can use it. I don't know if it
is good or bad - it's different, and I don't always like it. There are also
much more items that you have to carry to finish the game - earlier hacks
were nicer because the only absolutely necessary item was the amulet. Now
you have all the quest arifacts, bells etc, plus many new items (esp. in
the tool class) which can sometimes be useful - so you drag them around
filling the inventory and making it more difficult to play.

Unfair deaths: Perhaps the single item responsible for most unfair deaths
in 3.1 is the wand of sleep. The reason is, that its effects are
asymmetric: if you put a monster to sleep, it will wake up once you start
attacking it. If a monster puts you to sleep - you'll sleep as long as the
game decided, no matter what. So from my point of view the wand of sleep is
not a very efficient weapon - rather 'zap him and run' type. It is
therefore fairly common, and I usually find my first one before I even have
a chance of getting intrinsic sleep resistance or reflection. Unfortunately
in 50% of cases I find it in the hands of some monster - and it is almost
equivalent to a wand of death then... I already proposed to the DEV team to
give the player a chance (25% or so) of waking up when hit, but they are
reluctant to do it. Perhaps if more people vote for it? (or maybe make is
less common item, so that I have a chance to gain the intrinsic first?)

General: 3.1 concept is very nice, but the game became too long now. Some
of this comes from 'quantity instead of quality' approach - fort Ludios is
a typical example: If you can survive 10 soldiers, you will survive 200 as
well, and killing them all is just a boring hour of hacking (I mean you do
it, but you don't find any challenge). If there were some way of getting
around them - that would be a different story (or may be there is, but I
didn't find it? :-) Same thing with hell: the mazes offer no challenge to a
player who survived the castle (except for a chance for a 'stupid death') -
yet there are so many of them (3.1 is here better than 3.0 because of all
the special levels you can find, but still...). In the end, if I can spare
only a few hours a week for hacking, I end up playing one game several
weeks - nothing against it, mind you, but I'll vote against making 3.2 (or
4.0 - if it will ever be created) still richer and longer. My proposal from
now on - for every additional level take one away. For every new item -
remove some old one. Otherwise we'll end with an completely unplayable
monster instead of the wonderful game we had (you've seen the posts saying
'HACK 3.6 was better' - probably someone has his 'uplayability' level set
lower than I have).

These ae just some thoughts - fell free to disagree. I find 3.1 overall a 
very nice game - but in my opinion not all the changes go in the right
direction.

